# Root certificates the Pico wedge trusts (loaded by code.py). Lines starting with # are ignored.
# app.cowboymeats.com sits behind Cloudflare, which hands devices a certificate from one of
# several authorities (Google Trust Services, Let's Encrypt, Sectigo, SSL.com); Vercel behind it
# uses Let's Encrypt's 2025 'Generation Y' roots. The board's built-in list predates some of
# these, so every root any of them chains to is here. Sources: pki.goog, letsencrypt.org,
# and Mozilla's root store via curl.se/ca/cacert.pem (fetched 2026-10-22).
#
# Cloudflare, ECDSA chains (what a board usually gets)
